From: Andrew S Hall <ashall@magnus.acs.ohio-state.edu>
Subject: PSYCH:Myer-Briggs Nonsense

It is endlessly amusing to me to see normally sceptical and rational
people praising irrational garbage like the Myer-Briggs test just
because it agrees with their own prejudices about themselves.

The Myer-Briggs test is just another piece of voodoo psychology that
is about as useful as the flying yogis. Anyone with any knowledge
of psychology can answer the questions in such a way as to appear
to be any personality type. This also means that the test is highly
susceptible to what I would call the Walter Mitty syndrome. A completely
consvervative wallflower with a hyper-imagination would MB-Test as
a daring adventurer since his/her self-image would most closely
identify with those choices that reflect that personality. In short,
like all other psycho-babble bullshit tests, MB is worthless.

The way people go on about MB, I half expect to see some posts like
ASTRO:Extropians are Leos. It would make just as much sense.

Andrew Hall

